{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Hepta/pulls/821","id":5218567520,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVVyclM8AAAABNw0FYA","html_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Hepta/pull/821","diff_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Hepta/pull/821.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation/Hepta/pull/821.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Hepta/issues/821","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Hepta/pulls/821/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Hepta/pulls/821/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Hepta/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Hepta/issues/821/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TrillionniumFoundation/Hepta/statuses/e0c1ac3c97bb296e288de3d37b01f65d87772832","number":821,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat(hia): extend v15 checked semantics and qualify cold consumer recovery","user":{"login":"ProfHepta","id":102159240,"node_id":"U_kgDOBhbTiA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102159240?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta","html_url":"https://github.com/ProfHepta","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ProfHepta/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Why this change is needed\n\nThe source closure was missing scalar NDU evidence dependencies, the self-hosted compiler still rejected checked unsigned casts and Boolean equality, and the buffer lifecycle qualifier did not demonstrate independent consumer processes for the current compiler. The elapsed timeout fixture also anchored its clock before the collector started, so ordinary scheduling delay could distort the accelerated process deadline.\n\n## What this PR changes\n\n- Adds all 25 unsigned checked-cast type pairs and Boolean equality/inequality to the bounded v15 self-host profile, with rejection, trapping, fixed-point and mutation coverage.\n- Runs the existing compiler buffer lifecycle with independent consumer processes and adds a separate CI qualification for the current checked-in compiler while preserving the earlier frozen-source step.\n- Imports only the reviewed scalar-control changes and original evidence, validates frozen schedule prefixes and timing/accounting boundaries, and closes their release-source dependencies.\n- Anchors the elapsed test clock at the collector's first read. The production 60-second process and 2-second cleanup budgets and existing test-method counts are unchanged.\n- Excludes the current compiler's private SQLite authority state and its WAL/SHM files from CI artifacts, alongside the existing lifecycle exclusions.\n- Retains current-installation readback, the reconciled provider failure, all earlier failed qualification attempts, and the explicit lost-raw-data boundary.\n\n## Source and validation\n\nCurrent public head: `e0c1ac3c97bb296e288de3d37b01f65d87772832`, tree `082473de6403d058834e5a673d344874c4971680`. Its complete tree matches local `e7a5700b5542f3f8a921ad77b200c1db8a2cd445`.\n\nThe final native qualification was performed on clean local `b11d86085fba8084434ef5755eaea0794541f342`, whose tree `5e19c009c81acc86025c81a3dbdab14a4346b80f` exactly matches published `e6edab930cceb1216af2a0e2f27878e996879ad3`. The later commits change only two test fixtures, artifact upload exclusions and evidence. It does not relabel the native runs as observations of a different tree.\n\n| Validation | Observed result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Cold selfhost, original 180+3 second limits | PASS: 11/11 outer, 1,215/1,215 inner; 94.595 s |\n| Language coverage | PASS: 1,196/1,196 native, 1,183 scalar witnesses, 10/10 report assertions; 88.164 s |\n| Current v15 compiler buffer lifecycle | PASS_SCOPED_NONPRODUCTION_LIFECYCLE: 25 worker calls; 89.350 s |\n| Clock fixture follow-up | 3/3 original timeout tests, zero skips; 35.834 s |\n| Scalar evidence validator | 15/15 tests; offline replay of original 64 pairs / 128 cells / 307 objects |\n| Current public 2598 installation | Unchanged public checker matches worker/backend/catalog to exact lock bytes |\n\nFull scope and preservation receipts: [HIA_V15_QUALIFICATION_20261109.md](docs/HIA_V15_QUALIFICATION_20261109.md) and [qualification-summary.json](review-evidence/hia-v15-qualification-20261109/qualification-summary.json).\n\nFour complete raw archives retain 54,100 verified original files. The earlier ENOSPC failure, 9/10 stale-count assertion failure and SIGKILL attempt remain recorded; the SIGKILL attempt's unarchived temporary raw files were lost during environment recovery and are explicitly incomplete.\n\n## Remaining gates and claim limits\n\nCurrent-head hosted CI and review must pass before merge into the source branch. This is not a merge of the source tree into metadata main. A new default release lock must come byte-for-byte from the original successful CI artifact of the final merged source.\n\nOverall six-outcome acceptance remains HOLD. General Core and machine/ABI/resources/FFI/ISA/loader correctness, the original unfamiliar-Agent extension's separate semantic obligations and complete provider bill, candidate v15 installation, and stable NDU economic gain remain open. The historical scalar study observed 0/64 speed wins; it is not converted into a positive economic claim. The local same-Core lifecycle is not a replacement for the original unfamiliar-Agent trial.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-09T04:09:25Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T04:55:42Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"f2818ea1db25087fdf8d46fc1b3df86c69990767","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"TrillionniumFoundation:codex/hia-sixgap-source-closure-b850-20261109","ref":"codex/hia-sixgap-source-closure-b850-20261109","repo":{"id":1432132756,"node_id":"R_kgDOVVyclA","name":"Hepta","full_name":"TrillionniumFoundation/Hepta","owner":{"login":"TrillionniumFoundation","id":262513357,"node_id":"O_kgDOD6WizQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262513357?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation","html_url":"https://github.com/TrillionniumFoundation","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TrillionniumFoundation/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":null,"homepage":null,"language":"Python","visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":[],